    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d727">

                <pb facs="1040" n="1020" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg1020"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.9326/9–3050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in India
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-10-31T17:00:00-05:00">October 31, 1950—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>645. Pls ascertain and report nature response FonOff has recd from GOI tel to
                    Indian Amb Peiping (urtel 813, Sept 30).
                    Swedish FonOff has already indicated
                    willingness appoint Rep act in investigation charges U.S. bombing
                        Manchuria.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d727-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d727-f1" n="1" xml:id="d727-f1-content">
                <p>Ambassador Henderson transmitted the following reply in telegram 1130, dated
                    November 7:</p>
                <p>“Ministry External Affairs after careful search files (Deptel 645, October 31)
                    states last report from Panikkar this subject indicated CPR FonOff was studying matter. Panikkar had
                    reported previously his impression that Chou En-lai would not object if SC
                    should indicate desire send investigating committee. MEA doubts however whether Panikkar report any longer valid.”
                    (611.9326/11–750)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
